<!DOCTYPE suite SYSTEM "https://testng.org/testng-1.0.dtd">
<!-- PARALLEL EXECUTION: classes (not methods) + thread-count=2.
     The framework's shared state (ConfigReader, driver in BaseTest,
     ExtentManager, LocatorRepository) is all ThreadLocal/ConcurrentHashMap-backed
     and safe for concurrent classes. "methods" is deliberately NOT used:
     some test classes (e.g. BookStoreApplicationTest) keep page-object
     references in plain instance fields set up once and reused across
     that class's own @Test methods — TestNG normally shares ONE instance
     of a class across its methods, so running those methods concurrently
     on the same instance would race on those fields. "classes" gives each
     test class its own thread (and therefore its own driver, via
     BaseTest's ThreadLocal<WebDriver>) while keeping methods within a
     class sequential, which is safe with today's code as-is.
     Lowered from 3 to 2 (2026-08-07): DriverFactory.createWithPortConflictRetry()
     already retries the OS free-port TOCTOU race with jitter, budgeted for
     3+3=6 concurrent chromedriver launches (this suite runs alongside its
     sibling in Jenkins' "Run Tests Per Site" parallel branches) — but on a
     CPU-constrained shared box that budget was still getting exhausted
     repeatedly (8/8 attempts failing across several test classes in one
     run). 2+2=4 concurrent launches narrows the race window enough for the
     existing retry budget to actually cover it; raise back toward 3 only
     alongside a proportionally larger DRIVER_CREATION_MAX_ATTEMPTS if this
     box's CPU headroom improves. docker-compose.yml's SE_NODE_MAX_SESSIONS
     and pom.xml's surefire -Xmx2048m are independent of this value (they
     bound the Docker Selenium Grid path and JVM heap, not local
     ChromeDriver parallelism) — no need to keep those in lockstep with it.
     Override per-run with -Dtestng.thread-count=N if needed (or edit
     thread-count directly). -->
<suite name="SauceDemo Regression Suite" parallel="classes" thread-count="2">

  <!-- RetryListener is an IAnnotationTransformer — must be registered here
       (or via ServiceLoader), not via @Listeners on a test class, or it
       silently never fires. See BaseTest.java for the full explanation. -->
  <listeners>
    <listener class-name="com.automation.sites.listeners.RetryListener"/>
  </listeners>

  <test name="SauceDemo Regression Tests" preserve-order="true">
    <groups>
      <run>
        <include name="regression"/>
      </run>
    </groups>

    <packages>
      <package name="com.automation.sites.saucedemo.tests"/>
    </packages>

  </test>

</suite>
